{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "description": "DELIBERATELY WRONG copy used by test-shared-fixtures-break.sh. CabinetRows.build: groups the boxes in the cabinet into product rows under category sections. Filters (location, status of the box, then the search on the row name) apply before the row is built, so a row holds only the boxes that passed. Product key = GTIN, else the normalized name; a row is one (category, key). Row name = name of the most recently created box (then greater id). Row status = most urgent box (expired, expiringSoon, unknown, ok). Rows: status urgency, earliest expiry (month precision = last day of the month, none last), normalized name by code point, first box id. Boxes: expiry (none last), createdOrder, id. Sections: categoryOrder, then other categories by key, `uncategorized` always last. Box ids `bN` become UUIDs ending in N (zero-padded) so id order is numeric; `status` is given per box (the app supplies it from the expiry-status rule); `createdOrder` is a rank, not a date; locations are opaque labels.",
